Expected elements: present

All backbone items render: identity bar with `← demo` exiting to the chain, both stepping directions, scrubber, 128/1315 readout, phase rail; Code with a pinned line 32 (band + left rail + ⊙); Call Trace/Event Log as one tab strip with Call Trace open; Values below it, not in the strip; the `DATA` provenance row with its badge and sentences. Its tone does not contradict its label — blue reads informational, not success or error. Light here is a theme, not a register error: the surface is dense and tool-shaped, and the levels are re-derived rather than inverted (header #DDDDDD recessed under the #FFFFFF pane body, canvas #ECECEB, semantic tints are true light-mode 100/200 fills with 600–900 ink). Outside the three places named below, every static text pair I sampled measures ≥4.63:1.

The new fade is right to be conditional — Call Trace and Values, which do not overflow, show none. But its ramp (~29px) exceeds the 23px line pitch, so it always eats one whole legible line inside the box, and it masks the pane body rather than the ink, dissolving the RAW block's own surface. Cyan carries five meanings across four tokens, with two exact-hex collisions. Highest-priority fixes: shorten and rescope the fade; give the current iteration pill and the scrubber tick real contrast.

Rating: 6/10

